[thin] The lead-in narrows toward the 0.90 mm flat crest, which is raised 0.40 mm. This continuous taper spreads the leaf over the ledge during assembly.
alternatives: Thickening the ramp would shorten the usable lead-in or widen the four-bar bearing. Both change entry and catch contact at the actual receiver.
